<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Levellers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1640s</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Levellers were a radical political movement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/english-civil-war">English Civil War</a> era, led by John Lilburne, Richard Overton and William Walwyn. In pamphlets and the Agreement of the People they demanded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> of the people, a wide male franchise, religious toleration and equality before the law, debating them with army leaders at Putney in 1647. Cromwell crushed Leveller mutinies at Burford in 1649.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/levellers.jpg" alt="Levellers" width="172" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agreement_of_the_People_(1647-1649).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
